---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/layout/PageHeader.astro';

const lang = 'en';
const updated = 'June 2026';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" lang={lang}>
  <div class="container--blog">
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="Legal"
      title="Privacy policy"
      lead="What data this site handles and what rights you have."
    />

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
      <p>
        The data controller is Víctor Pariente González. You can exercise your rights or ask
        anything by writing to
        <a href="mailto:victor.pariente.gonzalez@gmail.com">victor.pariente.gonzalez@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What data is handled</h2>
      <p>
        This is a static site with no forms. The only way to share personal data is by
        choosing to email me, in which case I handle your email address and whatever
        information you include in your message.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Purpose and legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        I use that data solely to read and reply to your message. The legal basis is your
        consent when contacting me and my legitimate interest in keeping the conversation.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Retention</h2>
      <p>
        I keep emails for as long as needed to deal with your query and any relationship
        arising from it. After that, they are deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Recipients</h2>
      <p>
        I don't share your data with third parties. Email is handled through my email
        provider (Google), which acts as a data processor.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Cookies and storage</h2>
      <p>
        This site uses no tracking cookies and no analytics tools. It only stores your
        light/dark theme preference in your browser (via <code>localStorage</code>). That's
        strictly necessary technical storage for that feature, exempt from consent, and it
        never leaves your device.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can exercise your rights of access, rectification, erasure, objection,
        restriction and portability at any time by writing to the address above. If you feel
        they haven't been handled properly, you can lodge a complaint with the Spanish Data
        Protection Agency (<a href="https://www.aepd.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aepd.es</a>).
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
</style>
